    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>A transgender woman Embraced in the 1950s from prison after offering herself to a Vicissitude-using @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.6868ee8c357f4b73]{Sabbat} pack in exchange for the power to alter her form. She later diablerized that pack's leader and fled, eventually joining the Black Eagles through a shared interest in mortal targets. Her generation improved from 12th to 11th as a result of the diablerie.</p><p>See Richard B. Weinstein's entry for the pack's shared background as Black Eagle Consulting, Inc.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Angelica is guarded and pragmatic, having survived by seizing power when it was offered — even at terrible cost. She follows the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.paths-of-enlightenment.JournalEntry.n1ghtP4thOfN1ght]{Path of Night} and measures her actions against its Hierarchy of Sins rather than Humanity.</p><p><strong>Disciplines (as printed):</strong> Dominate 3, Obtenebration 3, Potence 2.<br><strong>Morality:</strong> @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.paths-of-enlightenment.JournalEntry.n1ghtP4thOfN1ght]{Path of Night} 4.</p>",
    "notes": "Convert Disciplines to owned power Items: Dominate 3, Obtenebration 3, Potence 2. Originally 12th generation; improved to 11th generation via diablerie per her background.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
